+## Implemented: entities and memberships
+
+Migrations `create_entities_table` and `create_entity_memberships_table`.
+
+| Table | Columns | Constraints |
+| ----- | ------- | ----------- |
+| `entities` | `id`, `name`, `slug`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at` | unique `entities_slug_unique (slug)`; soft deletes (a deleted entity keeps its slug reserved) |
+| `entity_memberships` | `id`, `entity_id`, `user_id`, `role` (default `employee`), `owner_seq` (stored generated), `created_at`, `updated_at` | FKs `entity_id` → `entities` and `user_id` → `users`, both cascade on delete; unique `entity_memberships_entity_user_unique (entity_id, user_id)`; unique `entity_memberships_one_owner (entity_id, owner_seq)` |
+
+- Routes bind entities by `slug` (`/e/{entity:slug}`); soft-deleted entities resolve to 404.
+- Soft deleting an entity does not fire the FK cascade, so the application deletes its memberships explicitly.
+- Roles are the `App\Models\UserRole` enum (`owner`, `admin`, `employee`); `manageable()` is `admin` + `employee`.
+- Authorization lives in `EntityPolicy` and `EntityMembershipPolicy`: only the owner manages settings; the owner's membership can never be deleted or reassigned through role assignment, only through ownership transfer.
